  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "A student runs three times as fast as she walks. She walked for 3 hours and ran for 2 hours and altogether travelled 36 km. What was her speed of walking?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$4\\text{ km/h}$",
      "worked": "Let $v$ km/h be her walking speed. Her running speed is $3v$ km/h. Using distance $=$ speed $\\times$ time,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3v+2(3v)&=36\\\\3v+6v&=36\\\\9v&=36\\\\v&=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nHer speed of walking was $4\\text{ km/h}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
